{"summary": "In this room, looking from the entrance, the warm walnut mid century modern desk, clean-lined and tapered, is centered on top of the muted taupe wool area rug, which is plush and subtly patterned. Flanking the desk are two deep teal geometric bookshelves, angular and modular, placed 0.5 meters to the left and right respectively. Adjacent to the desk is the matte black sleek side table, minimalist and frameless, displaying a matte terracotta ceramic vase, organic and slightly textured, along with two veined white marble coasters, smooth and circular. Two additional marble coasters rest on the desk. Above the left bookshelf hangs the first bold ochre abstract wall art, textured and dynamic, while the second piece is positioned above the desk, and the third above the right bookshelf. Suspended 1.2 meters above the desk is the polished brass pendant light, spherical and perforated, completing the refined retro aesthetic."}
```

